(
    """Negative fixture for execMotion: the same clip, stating no rate.

    The prose is a layer comment rather than `doc` on purpose; see
    sampled_clip.usda for why.

    The layer still carries `timeCodesPerSecond = 50` as metadata, and that is
    the whole point of this file: the number a computation would need is right
    there on the stage, `UsdStage::GetTimeCodesPerSecond()` reports it, and exec
    delivers none of it to a callback. So the only thing missing is the authored
    `motion:timeCodesPerSecond` attribute, and what motion.sampleAnimation does
    without it -- refuse to compile the request, or refuse at evaluation -- is a
    measurement this fixture exists to take."""
    doc = """Generated from Composed Stage of root layer C:\\dev\\usd-vrm-plugins\\plugins\\execMotion\\tests\\fixtures\\unrated_clip.usda
"""
    endTimeCode = 100
